# Line endings for duckstream.
#
# The package and its suites are LF, declared rather than assumed. They were
# mixed -- 52 LF against 19 CRLF across the repository, with one file mixed
# internally -- and that cost real time twice: a batch of edits written back
# through Python's text mode silently rewrote LF files as CRLF, inflating one
# review diff from ~2,000 lines to 4,600, and it later made a mutation audit's
# integrity check ambiguous between "a mutation leaked" and "the endings
# changed". Neither is a hard failure, which is exactly why it kept happening.
#
# Deliberately scoped to duckstream's own directories. The rest of this
# repository is somebody else's pipeline and normalising it here would be churn
# nobody asked for; `duckstream/` is destined to be extracted to its own
# repository, where this becomes a plain `* text=auto eol=lf`.

duckstream/** text=auto eol=lf
tests/** text=auto eol=lf
docs/duckstream/** text=auto eol=lf

# Parquet fixtures are written by the suites at runtime and never committed,
# but say so anyway: a text=auto that guessed wrong on binary would corrupt it.
*.parquet binary
